{
  "_comment": [
    "THE PARAMETERS REAL FABRIC ACCEPTS, cited per method. Contract 2 in",
    "docs/38-framework-conformance.md: a framework inspects a signature and",
    "declines to run if a parameter is missing, WITHOUT EVER CALLING IT.",
    "Accepting a parameter and ignoring it is correct emulation when there is",
    "nothing to switch; omitting it is not, because omission is the signal.",
    "",
    "EVERY ENTRY CARRIES ITS SOURCE. A reference assembled from memory would be",
    "the same defect one tier up: a claim about Fabric with nothing behind it.",
    "`source` is the page the signature was read from and `read` is that page's",
    "own last-updated date, so a stale entry can be found without re-reading",
    "every page.",
    "",
    "SCOPE IS NOW THE WHOLE DOCUMENTED SURFACE (docs/56 Phase 0). The module",
    "list is not ours: it is the table on the NotebookUtils overview page, so",
    "it can name a module nobody here thought to look for. That is the point --",
    "the previous `modules_not_yet_covered` field was an honest record of KNOWN",
    "absences and, by construction, could not list an unknown one.",
    "",
    "CITED IS NOT GRADED, and the two must not be confused. Every module below",
    "has a citation; `graded_by_contract_2` names the ones the live probe",
    "actually asserts, which is fewer. Reading a citation as a check is how a",
    "partial reference gets mistaken for coverage."
  ],
